import Vsa.Sim.ErrorSiteJal
import Vsa.Sim.DeriveCase
import Vsa.Sim.DecodeTable.Batch13Part15
import Vsa.Sim.Code.Eval_expr

/-!
# `DeriveErrorSite` — `#derive_error_site`, the Shape-B site multiplier (L6)

This is the `#derive_case` sibling for **error sites** (Shape B of
`experiments/exponentiation-endgame-design.md`). Every one of the 42
`jal runtime_error` error sites needs a per-site

```
T : Triple SitePre (fun c' => RuntimeErrorAt g inp m0 c')
```

that the landed error-site rows (`ErrorSiteRows`, `errRow`) currently take as a
HYPOTHESIS. `ErrorSiteJal.lean` already discharged the *tail half* of that work
ONCE, as the reusable combinator

```
jalStep_to_runtimeError … : Triple (JalErrPre g inp m0 pcJal b0 b1 b2 b3)
                                    (fun c' => RuntimeErrorAt g inp m0 c')
```

but instantiating it per site is still ~15 lines of boilerplate: the six
`by decide` well-formedness obligations, the `hword`/`htgtEq`
`BitVec.eq_of_toNat_eq; decide` bridges, and — the only genuinely per-site
argument — the `hdec` decode witness, assembled from that site's `DecodeTable`
lemma over `afterPrelude` with the three `GoodState`-supplied CSR pins
(`misa`/`cur_privilege`/`mseccfg`). `#derive_error_site` emits that whole
instantiation as one plain-term theorem, reducing the per-site jal-step artefact
to a single command line + the site's decode-lemma name.

## Command

```
#derive_error_site <name> pc <pcJal> word <word> imm <imm>
  bytes <b0> <b1> <b2> <b3> decode <decodeLemma>
```

emits

```
theorem <name> (g : (R : Register) → Option (RegisterType R))
    (inp : BitVec 64) (m0 : Std.ExtHashMap Nat (BitVec 8)) :
    Triple (JalErrPre g inp m0 <pcJal> <b0> <b1> <b2> <b3>)
      (fun c' => RuntimeErrorAt g inp m0 c')
```

`<decodeLemma>` is the site's `Vsa.Sim.DecodeTable.decode_<word>` theorem (the
one genuinely per-site input; everything else is boilerplate the command fills
in). The generated term is exactly the hand instantiation of
`jalStep_to_runtimeError` — see the demo below and the `example` at the bottom
that seq-composes it with a `#derive_case` prefix into the row's assumed `T`.

## Scope (honest)

This command emits the **jal-step** `Triple (JalErrPre …) (RuntimeErrorAt …)` —
the per-site tail. The *prefix* `Triple SitePre (JalErrPre …)` is a `#derive_case`
chain (`DeriveCase.lean`), and the seam that bridges a `#derive_case`
`SegEvalState` conclusion into `JalErrPre` (pinning `x10 = inp`, `mem = m0`, and
the `g` frame from the node's earlier dispatch) is genuinely per-site semantic
work — `ErrorSites.lean`'s header explicitly flags it as such, since the
`x10 = inp` fact is established BEFORE the prefix and is NOT recoverable from the
prefix segment generically. So this command deliberately does the uniform,
mechanical half (the jal step); the row assembles `T = Triple.seq <prefix>
<name>` once its prefix→`JalErrPre` marshalling is supplied (the bottom
`example` shows the composition abstractly).

NO `sorry`/`axiom`/`native_decide`/`bv_decide`; no Mathlib.
-/

open Lean Elab Command Term Meta
open LeanRV64DExecutable LeanRV64DExecutable.Functions Sail ConcurrencyInterfaceV1 Vsa
open Register
open Vsa.Machine (MState Config Step Steps)
open Vsa.Logic (Triple)

set_option maxHeartbeats 800000

namespace Vsa.Sim

/-! ## Syntax -/

/-- `#derive_error_site name (pc, word, imm) (b0, b1, b2, b3) decodeLemma` —
    emit the jal-step `Triple (JalErrPre …) (RuntimeErrorAt …)` for one
    `jal runtime_error` site, fully instantiating `jalStep_to_runtimeError` from
    the table. `(pc, word, imm)` is the jal's own decode data, `(b0..b3)` its
    little-endian bytes, `decodeLemma` its `DecodeTable.decode_<word>` theorem. -/
syntax (name := deriveErrorSiteCmd)
  "#derive_error_site " ident
    " (" term ", " term ", " term ")"
    " (" term ", " term ", " term ", " term ")"
    term:max : command

@[command_elab deriveErrorSiteCmd]
def elabDeriveErrorSite : CommandElab := fun stx => do
  match stx with
  | `(command| #derive_error_site $name:ident
        ($pc:term, $w:term, $imm:term)
        ($b0:term, $b1:term, $b2:term, $b3:term)
        $dec:term) => do
    elabCommand <|← `(command|
      /-- The jal-step `Triple` for this `jal runtime_error` site (generated by
      `#derive_error_site`): one machine step from the parked-at-`jal`
      precondition to the `runtime_error` entry, `jalStep_to_runtimeError`
      fully instantiated from the site's decode data. -/
      theorem $name (g : (R : Register) → Option (RegisterType R))
          (inp : BitVec 64) (m0 : Std.ExtHashMap Nat (BitVec 8)) :
          Triple (JalErrPre g inp m0 $pc $b0 $b1 $b2 $b3)
            (fun c' => RuntimeErrorAt g inp m0 c') :=
        jalStep_to_runtimeError g inp m0 $pc $w $imm $b0 $b1 $b2 $b3
          (by decide) (by decide) (by decide)
          (by decide)
          (by apply BitVec.eq_of_toNat_eq; decide)
          (fun σ hG =>
            $dec (afterPrelude σ)
              (by rw [get?_afterPrelude σ _ (by decide)]; exact hG.misa)
              (by rw [get?_afterPrelude σ _ (by decide)]; exact hG.cur_privilege)
              (by rw [get?_afterPrelude σ _ (by decide)]; exact hG.mseccfg))
          (by decide)
          (by apply BitVec.eq_of_toNat_eq; decide))
  | _ => throwUnsupportedSyntax

/-! ## Demo — the real site `jal runtime_error @ 0x800034e4`

Word `0x8c5ff0ef` = `JAL (0x1ff8c4, x1)`, target
`0x800034e4 + sext 0x1ff8c4 = 0x80002da8` (`runtime_error`'s entry). Bytes
(little-endian) `b0=0xef b1=0xf0 b2=0x5f b3=0x8c`. Decode lemma
`Vsa.Sim.DecodeTable.decode_8c5ff0ef`. -/

#derive_error_site errSite_800034e4
  (0x800034e4#64, 0x8c5ff0ef#32, 0x1ff8c4#21)
  (0xef#8, 0xf0#8, 0x5f#8, 0x8c#8)
  Vsa.Sim.DecodeTable.decode_8c5ff0ef

#print axioms errSite_800034e4

/-! ## Payoff — the row's assumed `T`, assembled from prefix + generated jal step

An error-site row's `T : Triple SitePre (RuntimeErrorAt g inp m0)` is now the
site's `#derive_case` prefix `Triple SitePre (JalErrPre …)` sequenced with the
`#derive_error_site`-generated jal step. The bespoke ~200-line per-site
marshalling collapses to one `Triple.seq` over two generated artefacts. -/
example (g : (R : Register) → Option (RegisterType R)) (inp : BitVec 64)
    (m0 : Std.ExtHashMap Nat (BitVec 8)) {SitePre : Vsa.Machine.Config → Prop}
    (prefix_seg :
      Triple SitePre (JalErrPre g inp m0 0x800034e4#64 0xef#8 0xf0#8 0x5f#8 0x8c#8)) :
    Triple SitePre (fun c' => RuntimeErrorAt g inp m0 c') :=
  Triple.seq prefix_seg (errSite_800034e4 g inp m0)

end Vsa.Sim
